(6091940, 896287, 116574, '<td valign="top">DNMC- A circle is not a Sphere,</td>', 'DNMC- A circle is not a Sphere,', '2010-07-14 01:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091945, 897295, 116574, '<td valign="top">that''s a circle not a sphere</td>', 'that''s a circle not a sphere', '2010-07-14 01:41:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091952, 897264, 116574, '<td valign="top">How is this a sphere and not just a circle.</td>', 'How is this a sphere and not just a circle.', '2010-07-14 01:46:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091958, 897263, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''ll assume that the spherical objects are a *certain* part of the foreground subject, because the circles on the background do not appear to be 3 dimensional.</td>', 'I''ll assume that the spherical objects are a *certain* part of the foreground subject, because the circles on the background do not appear to be 3 dimensional.', '2010-07-14 01:48:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091961, 897593, 83313, '<td valign="top">This is one case where dust on your reflective surface actually works for the shot!</td>', 'This is one case where dust on your reflective surface actually works for the shot!', '2010-07-14 01:49:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091962, 897622, 83313, '<td valign="top">Probably pushing the definition of spherical, but I''ll accept it.</td>', 'Probably pushing the definition of spherical, but I''ll accept it.', '2010-07-14 01:50:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091965, 897357, 116574, '<td valign="top">Olives are oval not spherical.</td>', 'Olives are oval not spherical.', '2010-07-14 01:52:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091966, 897400, 83313, '<td valign="top">Fits the challenge topic better than many of the other entries, but could use a little more visual oomph. I think some levels, curves, saturation and contrast could help it a bit.</td>', 'Fits the challenge topic better than many of the other entries, but could use a little more visual oomph. I think some levels, curves, saturation and contrast could help it a bit.', '2010-07-14 01:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091969, 897264, 66515, '<td valign="top">lol...I wanted to get a kaleidoscope for some fun shots. I never thought of using it for this challenge though.</td>', 'lol...I wanted to get a kaleidoscope for some fun shots. I never thought of using it for this challenge though.', '2010-07-14 01:54:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091972, 897622, 66515, '<td valign="top">Just to throw an idea out here. I think one of the defining features of a sphere is its ability to roll or at least be shaped like it could roll. Strangely I would call these balloon shaped rather than spherical. I know that would be a terrible way of describing the shape of a balloon but I hope you understand what I mean. <br/> <br/>Probably not voting on this one but that''s my 2 bits anyways</td>', 'Just to throw an idea out here. I think one of the defining features of a sphere is its ability to roll or at least be shaped like it could roll. Strangely I would call these balloon shaped rather than spherical. I know that would be a terrible way of describing the shape of a balloon but I hope you understand what I mean.  Probably not voting on this one but that''s my 2 bits anyways', '2010-07-14 01:58:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091973, 897286, 83313, '<td valign="top">I was debating how to vote on this one, as my first thought was that this is not a sphere. I looked it up on Wikepedia, and found this description as a subcategory of sphere:<br/><b><i>A sphere can also be defined as the surface formed by rotating a circle about any diameter. If the circle is replaced by an ellipse, and rotated about the major axis, the shape becomes a prolate spheroid, rotated about the minor axis, an oblate spheroid.</i></b> <br/> <br/>In spite of a very good shot of the eye, I anticipate you are going to get creamed by folks who will not take the time to look it up.</td>', 'I was debating how to vote on this one, as my first thought was that this is not a sphere. I looked it up on Wikepedia, and found this description as a subcategory of sphere:A sphere can also be defined as the surface formed by rotating a circle about any diameter. If the circle is replaced by an ellipse, and rotated about the major axis, the shape becomes a prolate spheroid, rotated about the minor axis, an oblate spheroid.  In spite of a very good shot of the eye, I anticipate you are going to get creamed by folks who will not take the time to look it up.', '2010-07-14 01:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091974, 896824, 66515, '<td valign="top">I am going to say this does meet the challenge. Other may not as the sphere shape is now um...a blob. Still, I think one of the problems with using a globe in this challenge is making it stand out and squishing it does that.</td>', 'I am going to say this does meet the challenge. Other may not as the sphere shape is now um...a blob. Still, I think one of the problems with using a globe in this challenge is making it stand out and squishing it does that.', '2010-07-14 02:00:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6091976, 897422, 83313, '<td valign="top">This has all the signs of being a <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=103142" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">VaWendy</a> entry.</td>', 'This has all the signs of being a  VaWendy entry.', '2010-07-14 02:01:57.000000', NULL, 1),
