(6099628, 897114, 119063, '<td valign="top">It''s totally a sphere, it just being affected by gravity.  If you chop up an apple and eat it, you''re still eating an apple vs. biting into an apple picked right off the tree.  <br/> <br/>Semantics strike again:<br/> <br/>According to challenge description: Your image should prominently feature one or more <u>spherical</u> (not just circular!) objects.<br/> <br/>Spherical definition:  <br/>1.	<br/>a.	Having the shape of a sphere; globular. <br/>b.	Having a shape <b>approximating</b> that of a sphere. <br/>2.	Of or relating to a sphere. <br/>3.	Of or relating to celestial bodies. <br/> <br/>Does anyone actually read the challenge descriptions?</td>', 'It''s totally a sphere, it just being affected by gravity.  If you chop up an apple and eat it, you''re still eating an apple vs. biting into an apple picked right off the tree.   Semantics strike again: According to challenge description: Your image should prominently feature one or more spherical (not just circular!) objects. Spherical definition:  1.	a.	Having the shape of a sphere; globular. b.	Having a shape approximating that of a sphere. 2.	Of or relating to a sphere. 3.	Of or relating to celestial bodies.  Does anyone actually read the challenge descriptions?', '2010-07-21 12:48:30.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6099635, 897114, 117474, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice capture. I haven''t really been able to catch a nice sequence of drops in a drip yet like you have on the top. <br/> <br/>I kinda have to agree with Bubbles that it isn''t really a sphere at first glance. It would be later, but in that shot it isn''t being a perfect sphere. I wonder if the knowledge that it would spherise itself later on was enough for most of the voters. <br/>I like the composition of the photo. I can''t really make out what''s being refracted in the drop though. It would have been really nice if I could. I can only imagine how tricky it would be though. Very nice background though. It''s nice and warm and good for the trops. <br/>I''m not convinced it''s in focus either. The drop we look at I mean. It''s nearly there but I''m not certain, and normally if you''re not certain it''s not, I''ve found.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-07-21 12:13:25.</i></td>', 'It''s a nice capture. I haven''t really been able to catch a nice sequence of drops in a drip yet like you have on the top.  I kinda have to agree with Bubbles that it isn''t really a sphere at first glance. It would be later, but in that shot it isn''t being a perfect sphere. I wonder if the knowledge that it would spherise itself later on was enough for most of the voters. I like the composition of the photo. I can''t really make out what''s being refracted in the drop though. It would have been really nice if I could. I can only imagine how tricky it would be though. Very nice background though. It''s nice and warm and good for the trops. I''m not convinced it''s in focus either. The drop we look at I mean. It''s nearly there but I''m not certain, and normally if you''re not certain it''s not, I''ve found.', '2010-07-21 13:01:59.000000', '2010-07-21 13:13:25.000000', 0),
(6099638, 897114, 117831, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 6. It isnt crisp as I think water shots should be and the angle is funky. Water drop shots are very popular and if you cant do them perfectly they tend to get ripped apart.</td>', 'I gave this a 6. It isnt crisp as I think water shots should be and the angle is funky. Water drop shots are very popular and if you cant do them perfectly they tend to get ripped apart.', '2010-07-21 13:03:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099639, 897114, 103142, '<td valign="top">You may have gotten hit by the "not perfect sphere" crowd (I had some of that on mine, as well). However, I think your biggest problem is that water drops have to be perfect on here. There''s been so many incredible drop shots, that it''s hard to get a decent score without perfection. It''s just that your drop is soft -- if the focus/stop motion was better, then the rest of the shot is quite nice. I love the background.</td>', 'You may have gotten hit by the "not perfect sphere" crowd (I had some of that on mine, as well). However, I think your biggest problem is that water drops have to be perfect on here. There''s been so many incredible drop shots, that it''s hard to get a decent score without perfection. It''s just that your drop is soft -- if the focus/stop motion was better, then the rest of the shot is quite nice. I love the background.', '2010-07-21 13:03:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099640, 897114, 67152, '<td valign="top">I voted this a 5 during voting being that it met the challenge. First, I like the offcentered crop and the color choice.  But, I think the image missed for a couple of reasons.   The speed of your shutter is probably one of the culprits for lower score than you wanted.  The edges of the water are not sharp and motion of the drops and water is creeping in to give the shot a slightly blurry appearance.  If you look at images by <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=52549" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">IreneM </a>and other masters of the water drop here at DPC, she uses 1/500 seconds.  She also has really perfected the lighting to get the images just so...plus she shoots and shoots and shoots until getting just the correct composition and effect and lighting.  Also, I would imagine a different, sharper and faster lens than the 18-200 would also be in order to really nail these type shots.  <br/> <br/></td>', 'I voted this a 5 during voting being that it met the challenge. First, I like the offcentered crop and the color choice.  But, I think the image missed for a couple of reasons.   The speed of your shutter is probably one of the culprits for lower score than you wanted.  The edges of the water are not sharp and motion of the drops and water is creeping in to give the shot a slightly blurry appearance.  If you look at images by  IreneM and other masters of the water drop here at DPC, she uses 1/500 seconds.  She also has really perfected the lighting to get the images just so...plus she shoots and shoots and shoots until getting just the correct composition and effect and lighting.  Also, I would imagine a different, sharper and faster lens than the 18-200 would also be in order to really nail these type shots.   ', '2010-07-21 13:03:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099646, 897114, 98339, '<td valign="top">Tristan...I gave you a 6 on this...in the upper right corner I see to much noise and I would have bumped it up more if your noise reduction was better, getting a good program like Neat Image or something like that would have made an amazing improvement on this...the other reason for my score is that the shot isn''t super clear and sharp (gotten to be a real stickler on this point).  <b>I didn''t really take off</b> because the drop on the bottom wasn''t "perfectly round/spherical" I got the general idea</td>', 'Tristan...I gave you a 6 on this...in the upper right corner I see to much noise and I would have bumped it up more if your noise reduction was better, getting a good program like Neat Image or something like that would have made an amazing improvement on this...the other reason for my score is that the shot isn''t super clear and sharp (gotten to be a real stickler on this point).  I didn''t really take off because the drop on the bottom wasn''t "perfectly round/spherical" I got the general idea', '2010-07-21 13:09:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099652, 897490, 67152, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work Irene.</td>', 'Beautiful work Irene.', '2010-07-21 13:13:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099743, 896893, 66515, '<td valign="top">Congrats on a) your personal best b) getting your first 6+ image. You did it far quicker than I did which brings me to my next point: I am a little jealous. =) Congratulations again!</td>', 'Congrats on a) your personal best b) getting your first 6+ image. You did it far quicker than I did which brings me to my next point: I am a little jealous. =) Congratulations again!', '2010-07-21 14:01:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099744, 897308, 103142, '<td valign="top">I actually found this quite cool -- I gave it a 7.</td>', 'I actually found this quite cool -- I gave it a 7.', '2010-07-21 14:01:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099781, 897605, 83149, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by boone168:</b></div><hr/><i> The cropping is too tight on those coloured balls. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yeah, I thought as much as well, but there was a silver can of diet coke on a table behind the balls that was a major distraction (and not removable with basic editing).  I was then forced to do the tight crop on top and tried to even out the image with a tight crop on the bottom as well.  Too bad I didn''t notice it while I was shooting.</td>', 'Originally posted by boone168: The cropping is too tight on those coloured balls.   Yeah, I thought as much as well, but there was a silver can of diet coke on a table behind the balls that was a major distraction (and not removable with basic editing).  I was then forced to do the tight crop on top and tried to even out the image with a tight crop on the bottom as well.  Too bad I didn''t notice it while I was shooting.', '2010-07-21 14:16:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099788, 897605, 83149, '<td valign="top">I don''t get it, I got two comments about none of the balls being in focus and one that likes the clarity of the cueball.  The cueball looks in focus to me on my laptop, which was the intention.</td>', 'I don''t get it, I got two comments about none of the balls being in focus and one that likes the clarity of the cueball.  The cueball looks in focus to me on my laptop, which was the intention.', '2010-07-21 14:19:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099862, 897491, 3936, '<td valign="top">Wow!!!  Congratulations on a well deserved Blue.  And, I''ve learned something new here today.  I''m looking forward to trying this out on my own.  Thank you for sharing the method.</td>', 'Wow!!!  Congratulations on a well deserved Blue.  And, I''ve learned something new here today.  I''m looking forward to trying this out on my own.  Thank you for sharing the method.', '2010-07-21 15:18:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099864, 897422, 3936, '<td valign="top">Very nicely done!  I am amazed by the detail and clarity of the image.  Whomever voted 1 on this shot, should have their keyboard taken away.  So should a few more that voted low also.  After reading the story, this moves from a really good image, to an amazing capture.</td>', 'Very nicely done!  I am amazed by the detail and clarity of the image.  Whomever voted 1 on this shot, should have their keyboard taken away.  So should a few more that voted low also.  After reading the story, this moves from a really good image, to an amazing capture.', '2010-07-21 15:22:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099866, 896804, 3936, '<td valign="top">Spectacular!  As one who is deathly afraid of heights, and cliffs, you get all the more credit for braving them just to get this image.  Absolutely beautiful.</td>', 'Spectacular!  As one who is deathly afraid of heights, and cliffs, you get all the more credit for braving them just to get this image.  Absolutely beautiful.', '2010-07-21 15:24:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099868, 897513, 3936, '<td valign="top">Yes, you probably would have done much better in the weathered challenge with this.  I think many voters did not see the spiral shell as a form of a sphere.  Sometimes the voters are much too literal.  The image does appear a little soft, as if the focus was not quite right, or it was magnified during cropping.  I do like your use of negative space here.  Perhaps a little more contrast on the lighting so the effect of the shell dissolving into the blackness would be even stronger.</td>', 'Yes, you probably would have done much better in the weathered challenge with this.  I think many voters did not see the spiral shell as a form of a sphere.  Sometimes the voters are much too literal.  The image does appear a little soft, as if the focus was not quite right, or it was magnified during cropping.  I do like your use of negative space here.  Perhaps a little more contrast on the lighting so the effect of the shell dissolving into the blackness would be even stronger.', '2010-07-21 15:29:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(6099905, 896893, 70503, '<td valign="top">Yeee hawwwwwwwwww!!! Well done!!!</td>', 'Yeee hawwwwwwwwww!!! Well done!!!', '2010-07-21 15:52:31.000000', NULL, 0),
